# Runtime state in an agent-team working tree.
#
# Everything below is created by agents or by the scion tooling during normal
# operation. None of it is human-authored, and none of it belongs in the repo.
# It is listed here so that `git clean` treats it as state to preserve rather
# than as junk to delete. On 2026-07-27 a routine working-tree reset destroyed
# the unlisted entries below, including a document that existed nowhere else.

# scion project/agent config. Written by the scion CLI, holds the project-id,
# name and slug, and (in normal operation) a state.yaml under it. It is a
# DIRECTORY in some environments and a FILE in others, so no trailing slash —
# this pattern must match both.
.scion

# Inbound message attachments and notes, delivered by `scion message --attach`.
# Filenames are channel-scoped (e.g. discord_<id>_<slug>.md) and the content is
# often the only copy in existence.
downloads/

# Per-role continuity files that long-lived agents keep in the workspace root.
# The `.<role>-state.md` convention is defined in templates/*/agents.md —
# currently `.coordinator-state.md` (templates/coordinator) and
# `.eng-manager-state.md` (templates/eng-manager). Matched by pattern rather
# than by name so a new role is protected the day its template lands, not the
# day someone remembers to update this file.
.*-state.md

# Local agent scratch directory: temporary artifacts and workspace-local briefs.
.scratch/
